From 17ad8e0dcb730e80471d424cc02d58afa11de205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:55:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qwen4exp: build the hyper-connection inject product with its
 input

The FFN mix's inject product is first read by the combine after the
experts, so it landed in the next GPU split, after the CPU expert phase.
There it quantized xn again and ran as its own 2-block launch. Put in the
graph when it is made, it sits in the split of the down product of the
same xn, and the CUDA backend runs both in one launch. Only the node
order changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6MCJC4HTKxvuGjKjqDuqQ
---
 src/models/qwen4exp.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp b/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
index 250eb74da..aa331db2e 100644
--- a/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
+++ b/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
@@ -362,6 +362,9 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_qwen4exp::graph::build_hc_mix(
     if (inject) {
         *inject = build_lora_mm(w_inject, xn);
         cb(*inject, "hc_inject", il);
+        // put it in the graph now, in the same GPU split as the down product of xn: its first reader
+        // comes after the experts, in the next split, where it would need its own quantized xn
+        ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, *inject);
     }
 
     return mixed;
